# Citation metadata for GPDI Analyzer.
# Zenodo reads this file when it archives a GitHub release and uses it to
# build the deposit record, so keep it in sync with every tagged release.
#
# The author block is deliberately a neutral placeholder, not a personal name.
# Zenodo reads this file when it builds a deposit and prints the author on the
# record, so a real name here would identify the authors while the manuscript
# is in masked review. Replace it with the authors, affiliations and ORCIDs
# only once the paper is accepted - in the same commit that adds the
# repository link to the availability statement. Do not archive a release
# while this placeholder is still in place.
#
# No DOI is listed. The software is cited by its repository and release
# (version 1.0.0); add a `identifiers` block only once a deposit has actually
# been made for THIS version.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "GPDI Analyzer"
abstract: >-
  GPDI Analyzer computes the Graded Poetry Difficulty Index (GPDI) for
  classical Chinese poetry. A poem is normalised to CJK characters, matched
  against a graded character inventory, and scored on four components:
  normalised average character difficulty (ACD*), high-difficulty character
  ratio (HDCR), out-of-vocabulary ratio (OOVR) and normalised text length
  (TL*). The tool also reports the character-level component on its own
  scale, a per-character profile, and the position of the text within a
  bundled reference corpus. It ships as a desktop application (PySide6) for
  Windows and macOS. Definitions, weighting and band boundaries are given in
  the associated study rather than in this metadata.
authors:
  - name: "GPDI Analyzer development team"
    # At acceptance replace the whole block with one entry per author, e.g.
    #   - family-names: "[…]"
    #     given-names: "[…]"
    #     affiliation: "[…]"
    #     orcid: "https://orcid.org/[…]"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-26"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/fancy61333/GPDI-Analyzer"
url: "https://github.com/fancy61333/GPDI-Analyzer"
keywords:
  - classical Chinese poetry
  - readability
  - text difficulty
  - graded vocabulary
  - Chinese as a second language
  - international Chinese language education
  - digital humanities
# Note for users: the graded character inventory and the reference corpus are
# not distributed with the software - see the README section "What is not
# included, and why".
